            <listPerson>
                <person xml:id="ALM01" sex="1">
                    <persName>
                        <roleName/>
                        <forename>John</forename>
                        <surname>Almon</surname>
                        <addName/>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1737-12-17">
                        <placeName/>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1805-12-12"/>
                    <occupation>bookseller and political journalist</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>Almon was a pamphleteer and publisher renowned for his courage in publishing work critical of the government. He was a great friend 
    and supporter of John Wilkes. He appears once in 1805 at a dinner at Philips's in March, but is mentioned again in Godwin's '1796' list.
    Given the relatively unusual name, his interest in political journalism, the connection to Philips, and the matching dates, 
    this identification seems solid.</p>
                        <p>See <title>DNB.</title></p>
                    </note>
                </person>
            </listPerson>
